{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassEndomorphism.rotation_step","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.rotation_step","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.rotation_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.rotation_step","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/rotation_step.lean#L35-L71","doc":"**The channel rotation, categorical (the `x ↦ ιx`, `q ↦ q̄` rotation).**\nA sequence `h` satisfies the odd-channel (non-compact, `𝔔_β`) step at\n`(q, x)` **iff** its `ι`-rotation `n ↦ ι^n·h_n` satisfies the\neven-channel (compact, binding) step at the bar-conjugated data\n`(σq, ιx)` — where `ι` is a formal square root of `−1` in the fibre\nring and `σ q * q = 1` is the division-free bar involution.\n\nThis is the generic form of Askey (1989) / Ismail–Masson\n`h_n(x|q) = i^{-n}·H_n(ix|q^{-1})`: **same eigenfunctions, rotated**;\nthe two channels of `𝔙` are one recurrence read through the rotation.\nNo `ℂ`: the archimedean instance `ι = Complex.I` is downstream of τ. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:channel-rotation-askey-lit","label":"rem:channel-rotation-askey-lit","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-endomorphism/channel-rotation-askey-lit.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.oddStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.oddStep","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/rotation_step.lean#L29-L33","doc":"Odd-channel (non-compact / `𝔔_β` / `q⁻¹`-Hermite) three-term step,\ndivision-free (multiplied through by `q^{n+1}`):\n`h_{n+2} = 2x·h_{n+1} + (1 − q^{-(n+1)})·h_n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.evenStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.evenStep","kind":"def","line":24,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassEndomorphism/rotation_step.lean#L24-L27","doc":"Even-channel (compact / binding / continuous q-Hermite) three-term step:\n`H_{n+2} = 2x·H_{n+1} − (1 − q^{n+1})·H_n`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}